VERDICT: SHIP WITH CHANGES (4)

The executable fix is correct. My four changes concern comments, coverage disclosures, and records; I do not require additional detector sessions.

I reviewed the pinned `987cb596`, since current HEAD has advanced. I independently recounted all 11 raw logs: every score and red-row list matches the packet. The detector has 27 vectors, 52 sessions, and nine mode discriminators. I checked the artifacts and code; I did not rebuild or rerun the emulator.

**Q1. The deletion is right and complete for #576.** `op1.f` is already decoded before the removed assignment. The same value reaches the same encoder and DRn stores afterward. No modeled FPSCR update changes, and the FD exception path—including its delay-slot variant—remains intact. Removing the cast also removes its undefined behavior for exceptional and out-of-range inputs; portable equivalence to that undefined behavior is not a meaningful promise.

**Change 1: tighten the product comment.** “Mis-copied” is an inference about provenance. Use “the same store FTRC makes, apparently copied,” or simply “an erroneous FTRC-style store.” Also prefer “FCNVSD preserves FPUL and writes its conversion result to DRn” over “writes DRn only”: architectural FCNVSD also has FPSCR cause/exception effects, which this patch does not implement. [SH-4 Software Manual, §9.29](https://www.renesas.com/en/document/mas/sh-4-software-manual)

**Q2. I find no open mandatory mutation cell under the stated DEPENDS-ON bound.** The base, verbatim reinstatement, and null-medium legs are demonstrably red. The body introduces no tested partition requiring additional destination or operand combinations. The measured conditional reinstatements provide useful additional coverage.

An escaping reinstatement nevertheless exists:

```c
if (ic->arg[0] == (size_t)&cpu->cd.sh.fr[4])
	cpu->cd.sh.fpul = (int32_t)op1.f;
```

At `FPUL=0x3fc00000`, PR=1, FD=0, executing `FCNVSD FPUL,DR4` changes FPUL to `1`. No existing FCNVSD row targets DR4. Its predicted 52/52 follows from the row destinations; this is not a newly measured score.

**Change 2: make the contract’s limits explicit.** The packet covers the FPUL channel across **{DR0, other than DR0}**, using DR2 as the second representative. It does not cover every destination. Converted values are read only at DR2; even DR0’s converted result is unchecked. Disclose that, the untested FD/PR and FPSCR state axes, and delay-slot behavior. Also include **exactly −2³¹** among unrowed FCNVSD inputs: its cast is defined, but that does not make it covered. Several newer scratch comments already make these corrections.

**Q3. A single-statement deletion suffices:** remove `FLOATING_POINT_AVAILABLE_CHECK;`.

All detector executions reach this handler with FD clear, so their results remain unchanged. With FD set, `FPUL=0x3fc00000`, and DR2 seeded with sentinels, the mutant converts and writes DR2 where the fixed handler raises the FPU-disable exception.

An FD=1 exception/readback row would catch this. The packet’s contract does **not** already disclose that omission; include it in change 2. This is outside the reachable body of the deleted FPUL store and does not establish an additional mandatory repair cell.

**Q4. The principal numerical records hold, but not every documentary assertion is established.**

**Change 3: qualify the timing and instrument provenance.** The scratch metadata shows:

- `PRETABLE.out` created at **17:17:41.526**.
- `base_head.raw` created at **17:17:43.651**, last modified at **17:18:13.244**.
